    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0424" n="398" xml:id="pg398"/>

                <head>204. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in India<anchor n="0" xml:id="d204-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-11-19T22:01:00-05:00">November 19, 1962,
                            22:01 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2167. Eyes Only for Ambassador. The following letter was delivered to the
                    President by the Indian Ambassador this evening, and is transmitted for your
                    information in the event that a copy has not been delivered to Embassy.
                    Department comments will follow in separate telegram.</p>
                <p>“New Delhi 19th November 1962.</p>
                <p>[This letter has not been declassified by the Indian Government. For a summary,
                    see <ref target="#d203">Document 203</ref>.]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d204-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
